From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opz Browser <opz@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:57:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tabs: private tabs in hidden one-off containers, next to
 normal tabs

"New private tab" in the New Tab button's popup opens the address bar card over the current tab and puts the pick in a new tab in a new hidden container (a userContextId from a range ContextualIdentityService never hands out, with no identity). Tabs opened from it share its container, and "New private tab in this session" in a private tab's context menu opens another tab in the same one. A new tab of a private session is moved next to the session's other tabs, and each session gets one outline around all of its tabs plus a mask badge on each icon, in the session's color, collapsed and expanded.

Private tabs keep no global history (disableglobalhistory on their browser), are left out of session store files, closed tabs and closed windows, tab sync, urlbar search and input history, form history and download history. When the last tab of a hidden container is gone its data is wiped; ids that may hold data are listed in opz-private-tabs.json in the profile and wiped at the next start after a crash. The logic is in browser/modules/OpzPrivateTabs.sys.mjs.
